+
+**Formulas:**
+The piecewise linear interpolation between adjacent nodes $(s_i, \alpha_i)$ and $(s_{i+1}, \alpha_{i+1})$ evaluates opacity $\alpha$ for a scalar value $s$ as:
+$$\alpha(s) = \alpha_i + \frac{\alpha_{i+1} - \alpha_i}{s_{i+1} - s_i}(s - s_i), \quad \text{for } s_i \le s < s_{i+1}$$
+where $s$ is the input scalar/gradient value, and $\alpha_i, \alpha_{i+1}$ are the opacities of the bounding nodes [G].
 
